WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Module review · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Recap: MEAL

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Your MEAL framework links your Theory of Change to evidence, learning and decisions from day one.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
You built evidence into your idea from the start: a results framework with indicators, baselines and targets, ethical data collection, ways to listen to the people you serve and routines to learn and report.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
One lesson at a time

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:38.881
6.1 MEAL principles and a proportionate system: MEAL exists to inform real decisions, and it should be sized to what you can keep up.

6
00:00:38.881 --> 00:00:49.370
6.2 From Theory of Change to results framework: A results framework turns your Theory of Change into a table of results, evidence and assumptions.

7
00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:59.007
6.3 Indicators: A good indicator is clearly defined, measurable and relevant, so everyone would measure it the same way.

8
00:00:59.407 --> 00:01:00.007
One lesson at a time

9
00:01:00.007 --> 00:01:09.385
6.4 Baselines and targets: Without a baseline you cannot show change; for something new, now is the moment to capture it.

10
00:01:09.385 --> 00:01:18.763
6.5 Data collection, ethics and data quality: A simple, credible method used ethically and consistently beats a sophisticated tool nobody opens.

11
00:01:18.763 --> 00:01:29.881
6.6 The MEAL plan and budget: The MEAL plan is the short operating manual for your evidence: roles, timing, reviews, budget and reporting.

12
00:01:30.281 --> 00:01:30.881
One lesson at a time

13
00:01:30.881 --> 00:01:41.000
6.7 Monitoring: planned versus actual: Monitoring compares planned with actual; in a first pilot, even two or three data points reveal a lot.

14
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:49.637
6.8 Evaluation: Evaluation asks whether, why and for whom it works; for something new, relevance and effectiveness matter most.

15
00:01:49.637 --> 00:02:00.756
6.9 Accountability: participation, feedback and complaints: Listening to the people you serve and handling complaints fairly respects their dignity and improves the work.

16
00:02:01.156 --> 00:02:01.756
One lesson at a time

17
00:02:01.756 --> 00:02:11.504
6.10 Learning and adaptive management: Learning turns evidence into better decisions; it is how you find out what works before you grow.

18
00:02:11.504 --> 00:02:21.511
6.11 Reporting and communicating evidence: Different audiences need different reports, from short dashboards for co-founders to accessible feedback for communities.

19
00:02:22.111 --> 00:02:34.711
Your evidence gives your brand credibility and supplies the proof points for your communications; your indicators and reviews also feed the financial and risk decisions in Protect.

20
00:02:35.311 --> 00:02:40.111
You check your MEAL framework and download each exercise as a PDF.

21
00:02:41.611 --> 00:02:44.711
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
